The robot's expressions are handled by the roboEyes library. You can change how it reacts to the world in the setup() and loop() sections.

Change Moods
In the loop(), you currently have it set to HAPPY when touched. You can change the expressions to:

DEFAULT

TIRED

ANGRY

HAPPY

Example Code Change:
if (digitalRead(touchSensor) == HIGH) {
  roboEyes.setMood(ANGRY); // Change this from HAPPY to ANGRY
}

Enable Animations
You can trigger "one-shot" animations when an event happens (like hitting an obstacle):

roboEyes.anim_confused(); (Eyes shake left and right)

roboEyes.anim_laugh(); (Eyes shake up and down)
